163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (         The Sedek are one of the indigenous peoples of Taiwan, mainly found in Nantou and Hualien Counties. Known for their traditional tattoos, clothing, and art, the Sedek are a brave and passionate people, and have been widely discussed for their participation in the production of the movie "Sedek Barai". The Qingliu tribe is one of the most important settlements of the Sedek tribe and is located in the Mutual Aid Village in Renai Township, Nantou County. The area is mainly inhabited by the surviving clans and their descendants who survived the Wushe incident and were forcibly relocated there by the Japanese government at the time. The area is surrounded by the Beigang and Meibara Rivers, so it was once called "Chuanzhong Island" during Japanese rule.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
164 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (         The most famous attraction in the tribe is the Wusha Incident Memorial Hall. The memorial hall is made of two floors of masonry, and the black and white patterns on the exterior show the unique ethnic art of the Sedek people. Inside the museum, artifacts and pictures are displayed to explain the events of the Wushe incident, and costumes and props from the film "Cedric Barlet" are also on display. In the museum, there is a special docent to explain the incident and a cultural experience course, so that every visitor to the museum can have a clearer understanding of what happened.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
