322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (      The Wushe incident profoundly impacted the indigenous peoples of the time and the government's policy toward the indigenous people. First, the Wushe Incident caused significant damage to the Seediq tribe, resulting in heavy casualties and destruction of the tribe, and forced relocation to Chuanzhong Island. This incident revealed the discrimination and oppression faced by the indigenous people and reflected the mistrust and conflict between the indigenous people and the government.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (       Mona Rudo and other Seediq warriors sacrificed their lives to defend their culture and traditions. The incident reveals the importance and persistence of the indigenous people in their own culture and highlights the failure of the policies of the time to protect the rights and cultural heritage of the indigenous people.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (        Eventually, the Wushe Incident aroused international concern and the colonial government of the time gradually adjusted its policy towards the Aborigines in response to international pressure, gradually shifting its policy to protect and develop the culture of the Aborigines and to fight for more rights for the aborigines in Taiwan.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
